The EC explained its ongoing process of equivalence assessment on audit, including reactions to its consultation document issued in January;
The JFSA emphasized the importance of maintaining the openness in the European market in proceeding with the equivalence assessment, and detailed the features of Japanese auditor oversight system.
Both parties also discussed about other recent developments and possible cooperations in the area of auditor oversight, with a view to maintaining the openness in the both markets.

Collaborating to identify joint research startups between Japan and Canada through grants or matching schemes;
Promoting joint research and development activities between Japan and Canada by utilizing the Global Research and Development Center for Business by Quantum-AI technology (G-QuAT) in the National Institute of Advanced Industrial Science and Technology (AIST), etc.;
Strengthening collaboration by promoting joint research among research institutes and companies in Japan and Canada for the exchange and development of human resources and utilizing international conferences, workshops, and seminars;
Supporting effective standards setting relevant to industrial science and technology through information sharing, etc.;
Pursuing cooperative projects through the newly established Japan-Canada Industrial R&D Policy Dialogue; etc.

Promoting existing public support in both countries for investment and other efforts in Canada by Japanese companies;
Promoting mutual understanding between Japanese companies and relevant regulatory authorities in Canada;
Promoting the establishment of meaningful relationships between Japanese companies and indigenous peoples in Canada;
Collaboration in times of emergency in battery supply chains, including with respect to critical minerals;
Promoting the use of renewable energy in battery supply chains;
Discussing international standards, such as those on carbon footprint calculation; etc.

